Colonel
I'm not going to sugarcoat this.
Your wife is in critical condition, her sickness is unknown.
We've tried everything. There's only one option left.

Me
I figured as much. What is it? What's the plan?

Colonel
We miniaturize you. Down to the size of a single cell.
We inject you into her bloodstream.
You'll be the cure - from the inside.

Me
Wait, what? That's insane.
You can't just shrink a person! That's science fiction!

Colonel
Not anymore. We've tested it on animals.
The tech works. But we've never tried it on a human.
Let alone in a live medical emergency.

Me
No trial run? You're just throwing me in?

Colonel
Yes. Time's running out. The virus is spreading.
Her immune system is failing. This is your only shot.
Kill every trace of the virus before her system collapses.

Me
And if I die in there?

Colonel
Then you die in there. But if you don't go.. she dies out here.

Me
You said she doesn't have time. How long?

Colonel
Hours. Maybe less.

Me
..Then let's do it.

Colonel
One more thing.
You'll have a surgicaly-modified shotgun.
Designed to break through corrupted cells and infected tissue.

Colonel
Your goal is to clear a path by destroying corrupted walls.
These block your progress and are spreading the infection.
Just be careful where you point it..
Shoot the wrong wall -one that's healthy- and she loses health.

Me
So I have to fight carefully.
One wrong move, and I hurt her even more.

Colonel
Exactly. And even if you do everything right,
her health will keep dropping slowly over time.
She's sick. The virus is attacking her constantly.

Me
I'll be quick.
Tell her I love her..

Colonel
You'll tell her yourself when you get out of here alive..
(Hopefully).

Technician
Injection ready, sir.

Colonel
Godspeed, Sergeant.
